"hero": "\n<section class=\"page-hero\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\">{{ppp:breadcrumbs}}<span class=\"eyebrow\">Ellis Services Group · Perth</span><h1>Switchboard Repairs &amp; Upgrades Perth</h1><aside class=\"intent-safety\" data-intent-safety><p><strong>Electrical danger comes before booking.</strong> For a shock or tingling tap, keep clear and call <a href=\"tel:131351\">Western Power 13 13 51</a>. For a life-threatening emergency or fire, call <a href=\"tel:000\">000</a>. <a href=\"https://www.westernpower.com.au/issues-enquiries/reporting-incidents-and-emergencies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official emergency guidance</a>. For loss of supply, check <a href=\"https://www.westernpower.com.au/issues-enquiries/reporting-issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Western Power outage reporting</a> before assuming an internal circuit fault.</p></aside><p class=\"expanded-lead\">Switchboard repairs and upgrades in Perth, following assessment of the existing installation, reported faults and proposed loads. We explain the findings and quote for the agreed scope rather than assuming every older board needs full replacement.</p><p><a class=\"button\" href=\"tel:0413477667\">Call 0413 477 667</a> <a class=\"button service-book-button\" href=\"contact.html?service=switchboard-upgrades-perth.html\">Arrange a visit &amp; quote</a></p><p class=\"expanded-hours\">Routine service hours: 09:00–21:00, seven days a week. 24-hour emergency repairs are available; call to confirm attendance arrangements and the quoted emergency work. No arrival time is guaranteed.</p><nav aria-label=\"On this page\" class=\"expanded-toc\"><a href=\"#service-scope\">Service scope</a><a href=\"#service-scenarios\">Common situations</a><a href=\"#service-quote\">Process &amp; quote</a><a href=\"#service-faq\">FAQs</a></nav></div></section>" as TrustedHtml,
"sections": [
{
"id": "section-1",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-scope\">Switchboard upgrades Perth: service scope</h2><ul><li>Assess switchboard faults and proposed upgrade requirements.</li><li>Quote for the agreed board, protection devices, circuit work and testing.</li><li>Identify supply coordination, access, interruptions and required documentation for the actual work.</li><li>Whole-house rewiring, utility works and remediation of unidentified concealed faults are not automatically included in a board upgrade.</li></ul><p>We confirm the property, installation and requested outcome before selecting the work. Fixed plumbing and electrical tasks are handled by the appropriate qualified trade; a coordinated visit does not make every task interchangeable. Current documentation relevant to the proposed work can be requested privately.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"electrical.html\">Perth electrical services</a></li><li><a href=\"power-faults-perth.html\">Fault finding before equipment replacement</a></li><li><a href=\"safety-switch-tripping-perth.html\">Safety switch faults</a></li><li><a href=\"rcd-testing-perth.html\">RCD testing and findings</a></li><li><a href=\"power-points-perth.html\">New outlet requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"service-areas.html\">Perth service regions</a></li></ul></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-2",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section expanded-scenarios\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-scenarios\">Common situations and what to report</h2><div class=\"expanded-scenario\"><h3>An older fuse board and new kitchen appliances</h3><p>You are adding equipment to a home with an older board. Describe the proposed appliances and existing concerns without opening the board. Capacity, protection and connection requirements need assessment; the age or appearance alone does not define the required upgrade.</p></div><div class=\"expanded-scenario\"><h3>Repeated trips or signs of damage</h3><p>A trip may arise from a circuit or connected equipment rather than a failed switchboard. An upgrade is not a substitute for fault finding. Burning, sparking, smoke or shock needs safety-first action, not repeated attempts to reset devices.</p></div><p>These are illustrative situations, not customer case studies or diagnoses. Report what you have noticed; you do not need to identify the cause before contacting us.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-3",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-quote\">Assessment, work plan and written quote</h2><ol class=\"expanded-steps\"><li><strong>Describe the job.</strong> Give the suburb, affected equipment or planned installation, when it began and whether the condition is worsening. Add safe access and the person who can approve the work.</li><li><strong>Assess the installation.</strong> We check the relevant equipment and connections on site. Concealed work, product compatibility and the cause of a fault cannot be guaranteed from an enquiry or photograph.</li><li><strong>Agree the scope.</strong> The written quote identifies attendance or investigation, the selected equipment, materials and agreed work. Confirm GST, disposal, access, testing and any making good that applies to the specific job.</li><li><strong>Approve changes separately.</strong> If findings change the required work, we explain the additional scope and charge before proceeding. Confirm the checks and completion information needed for a rental or managed property.</li></ol><p>Published standard-hours guide ranges elsewhere on this site are not a fixed price for this unseen job. Emergency repair charges follow the quoted plan. There is no assumed free attendance, unlimited investigation or universal hourly rate.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "service-faq",
"kind": "faq",
"container": "\n<section class=\"section faq\" id=\"service-faq\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2>Switchboard Repairs &amp; Upgrades Perth FAQs</h2><!-- site-intent:start --><div class=\"intent-content\" data-site-intent><h3>Prepare the request and approval</h3><p>Give the property location, observable symptoms or intended installation, access contact and the person who can approve the work. The agreed quote sets out the assessment and work; submitting a form does not reserve an appointment.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"electrical.html\">Perth electrical services</a></li><li><a href=\"power-faults-perth.html\">Fault finding before equipment replacement</a></li><li><a href=\"safety-switch-tripping-perth.html\">Safety switch faults</a></li><li><a href=\"rcd-testing-perth.html\">RCD testing and findings</a></li><li><a href=\"power-points-perth.html\">New outlet requirements</a></li></ul></div><!-- site-intent:end --><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:0:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:0:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:1:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:1:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:2:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:2:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:3:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:3:answer}}</details></div></section>" as TrustedHtml,
